# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .gitignore — demo-data-seeder
#
# A Node (ESM) + SFDX data-tooling repo. It GENERATES realistic, narrative-rich
# Salesforce Sales Cloud demo data (Accounts/Contacts/Opps/Emails/transcripts/
# activities) and loads it into Salesforce scratch / dev / customer orgs.
#
# Ignore three classes of cruft: (1) Node/SFDX toolchain state, (2) generated
# data outputs + per-run manifests (org-specific, disposable, never portable),
# (3) secrets / org auth material. Commit source + scenario configs + docs only.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Node / npm ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.npm/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/
.node_repl_history
*.tgz
.eslintcache
.cache/
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ── Salesforce CLI / SFDX ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local CLI state, retrieved/temp metadata, and per-developer config. The org
# auth itself lives in ~/.sfdx (outside the repo), but these land in-tree.
.sf/
.sfdx/
.localdevserver/
deploy-options.json
**/__tests__/**/*.log

# SFDX scratch-org definitions are SOURCE (config/*-scratch-def.json) and ARE
# committed. Only ignore generated/local org artifacts:
.sfdx-data/
*.sfdx-org

# ── Generated demo-data outputs ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Everything the seeder emits is org-specific and reproducible from source +
# scenario config — never commit it. See tradeoffs in the seeder docs.
/out/
/generated/
/dist/
/build/
/tmp/
*.local
*.local.*

# Per-run created-record manifests (created-record IDs for cleanup/teardown).
# Org-specific + stale the moment the org is reaped — disposable, not portable.
.manifest.json
*.manifest.json
manifest-*.json

# Large generated dataset dumps: bulk LLM-generated email/transcript/note
# bodies, anchor-company caches (Wikidata/SEC/EDGAR pulls), bulk-loader payloads,
# and eval result snapshots written per run.
/data/generated/
/anchors-cache/
*.dataset.json
*.dataset.ndjson
*.bulk.csv
**/results/*.json
eval-results/

# ── Secrets / keys / org auth material ───────────────────────────────────────
# A seeder authenticates to live orgs and may route LLM calls — keep every
# credential out of git. .env files, JWT/connected-app keys, auth URLs.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.jks
server.key
jwt/
*.auth-url
*sfdxAuthUrl*
authFiles/

# ── Editor / IDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.project
.classpath
.settings/
*.sublime-project
*.sublime-workspace

# ── OS cruft ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ── Claude Code (agent-side) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .claude/settings.json is committed config. Per-developer local settings and
# the MCP config (which names YOUR org alias) stay out of git — see
# docs/target-orgs.md for the .mcp.json snippet.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/local/
.claude/*.local.log
.mcp.json

# Built front-end bundle — build output, never committed.
apps/web/dist/

# local introspection artifacts (CapabilityProfiles)
.dataseed/
